+{
+  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
+  "title": "Sail editor diagnostic stream record v1",
+  "oneOf": [
+    {
+      "type": "object",
+      "additionalProperties": false,
+      "required": [
+        "protocol",
+        "version",
+        "event",
+        "severity",
+        "code",
+        "message",
+        "span",
+        "related",
+        "fixes"
+      ],
+      "properties": {
+        "protocol": {
+          "const": "sail-editor-diagnostics"
+        },
+        "version": {
+          "const": 1
+        },
+        "event": {
+          "const": "diagnostic"
+        },
+        "severity": {
+          "enum": [
+            "error",
+            "warning",
+            "information",
+            "hint"
+          ]
+        },
+        "code": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "minLength": 1
+        },
+        "message": {
+          "type": "string"
+        },
+        "span": {
+          "anyOf": [
+            {
+              "$ref": "#/$defs/span"
+            },
+            {
+              "type": "null"
+            }
+          ]
+        },
+        "related": {
+          "type": "array",
+          "maxItems": 128,
+          "items": {
+            "type": "object",
+            "additionalProperties": false,
+            "required": [
+              "span",
+              "message"
+            ],
+            "properties": {
+              "span": {
+                "$ref": "#/$defs/span"
+              },
+              "message": {
+                "type": "string"
+              }
+            }
+          }
+        },
+        "fixes": {
+          "type": "array",
+          "maxItems": 32,
+          "items": {
+            "$ref": "#/$defs/fix"
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "object",
+      "additionalProperties": false,
+      "required": [
+        "protocol",
+        "version",
+        "event",
+        "success",
+        "diagnostics"
+      ],
+      "properties": {
+        "protocol": {
+          "const": "sail-editor-diagnostics"
+        },
+        "version": {
+          "const": 1
+        },
+        "event": {
+          "const": "summary"
+        },
+        "success": {
+          "type": "boolean"
+        },
+        "diagnostics": {
+          "type": "integer",
+          "minimum": 0
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  ],
+  "$defs": {
+    "span": {
+      "type": "object",
+      "additionalProperties": false,
+      "required": [
+        "file",
+        "byteStart",
+        "byteEnd",
+        "sourceHash"
+      ],
+      "properties": {
+        "file": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Absolute physical host path, preserving the supplied spelling."
+        },
+        "byteStart": {
+          "type": "integer",
+          "minimum": 0
+        },
+        "byteEnd": {
+          "type": "integer",
+          "minimum": 0
+        },
+        "sourceHash": {
+          "type": "object",
+          "additionalProperties": false,
+          "required": [
+            "algorithm",
+            "value"
+          ],
+          "properties": {
+            "algorithm": {
+              "const": "fnv1a64"
+            },
+            "value": {
+              "type": "string",
+              "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{16}$"
+            }
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    },
+    "fix": {
+      "type": "object",
+      "additionalProperties": false,
+      "required": [
+        "title",
+        "edits"
+      ],
+      "properties": {
+        "title": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "minLength": 1
+        },
+        "edits": {
+          "type": "array",
+          "minItems": 1,
+          "maxItems": 128,
+          "items": {
+            "type": "object",
+            "additionalProperties": false,
+            "required": [
+              "span",
+              "oldText",
+              "newText"
+            ],
+            "properties": {
+              "span": {
+                "$ref": "#/$defs/span"
+              },
+              "oldText": {
+                "type": "string"
+              },
+              "newText": {
+                "type": "string"
+              }
+            }
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  },
+  "$comment": "The implementation additionally validates absolute host paths, byte order/bounds, UTF-8 boundaries, source hashes, edit overlap, located fixes, stream order/count and exit-status consistency."
+}
diff --git a/doc/editor-diagnostics.md b/doc/editor-diagnostics.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..4e0799938
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/editor-diagnostics.md
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Editor diagnostic stream (proposal, version 1)
+
+This companion implementation is an upstream review proposal. It is not a
+claim that a released Sail compiler implements the interface. Apply it after
+check-context v1; the two protocols negotiate independently.
+
+`--diagnostics-format-version` prints `1` and exits without loading sources.
+`--diagnostics-format json-v1` enables the stream and implies check-only mode.
+Clients must negotiate before adding the format option. Unsupported versions
+must remain visible when JSON was explicitly requested; an automatic client
+can use the existing terminal renderer when the protocol is unavailable.
+
+Stdout contains UTF-8 newline-delimited JSON conforming to
+[the schema](editor-diagnostics-v1.schema.json). Stderr remains available for
+process/infrastructure errors. The normal terminal renderer is unchanged when
+the option is absent. Interactive/backend output should not be combined with
+this check-only interface.
+
+Each diagnostic has a severity, stable code, message, nullable primary span,
+related locations and fixes. Generated or virtual sources without a physical
+location use `span: null`; clients must show their messages as global findings
+rather than inventing a file or reporting a clean check.
+
+Spans use absolute physical paths and zero-based UTF-8 byte offsets with an
+exclusive end. Path spelling is preserved; no filesystem canonicalization is
+required. `sourceHash` is the 64-bit FNV-1a fingerprint of the exact loaded
+source bytes, represented as 16 lowercase hexadecimal digits. Its purpose is
+source identity, not cryptographic authentication. CRLF and trailing newlines
+participate in the hash. Files are read in binary mode so the contract does
+not depend on host text-mode newline translation. Clients check the fingerprint
+and byte boundaries before converting to their negotiated position encoding.
+
+A fix is a title and 1..128 plain-text edits. Each edit includes a span with its
+source hash, `oldText` and `newText`. Edits must not overlap, including two
+insertions at the same offset. A fix is indivisible: clients validate every
+source, old text and range before offering it, and repeat validation at resolve.
+Versioned editor edits should be used for open documents. The initial producer
+attaches a value-preserving lowercase fix to the mixed-case hexadecimal-literal
+warning, using its AST location rather than interpreting an English message.
+Other diagnostics can expose fixes incrementally; absence of fixes is explicit.
+A warning promoted by `--warn-error` currently uses the fatal error interface
+and does not retain the ordinary warning's fixes.
+
+Exactly one final summary is required, even when there are no diagnostics.
+It gives the diagnostic count and success flag; the flag must agree with the
+process exit status and cannot be true after an error diagnostic. A stream with
+missing/duplicate summaries, wrong counts, unsupported records, invalid spans,
+or truncated output is a failed check. An unexpected exception or early exit
+after enabling the format emits a failure summary, never an empty success.
+
+Pure serialization, hash, UTF-8/CRLF and invalid-span tests live in
+`test/unit/test_editor_diagnostics.ml`. Build and run:
+
+```sh
+dune build --release src/bin/sail.exe
+SAIL_UNIT_TESTS=true dune runtest --release test/unit
+_build/default/src/bin/sail.exe --diagnostics-format-version
+_build/default/src/bin/sail.exe --diagnostics-format json-v1 --just-check model.sail
+```
+
+The compiler continues to stop at its existing fatal error boundary; this
+protocol does not imply multiple-error recovery. Context configuration, source
+selection and type-checking behavior remain owned by the compiler.
